## B F1: the review-artifact gate

The write path in `applyArchitectureReconciliation` now calls
`assertReviewedStagedDelta` before the write-set guard. The gate reads the
staged manifest from the preview transaction plan. It refuses the write when
the staged manifest stages a non-empty baseline delta, holds no review record,
and its status is not `accepted`. An accepted manifest passes. A write that
stages no delta passes.

The new file `packages/architecture-enforcement/src/__tests__/architecture-review-gate.test.ts`
holds four cases. The first case proves that an unreviewed candidate write
with a staged delta is refused. The second case proves that a reviewed
candidate write passes. The third case proves that an accepted manifest
passes. The fourth case proves that a candidate write without a delta passes.

### The review record was not added

The orchestrator asked for a review entry in the committed v2 manifest that
cites the review artifacts of this phase. The v2 schema cannot hold that
entry. Two rules block it:

- `packages/architecture-enforcement/src/v2-manifest-validation.ts:631` requires
  `evidencePath` to equal `REVIEW_EVIDENCE_PATHS[index]`, which names the
  review folder of another track. That folder holds no files today.
- `packages/architecture-enforcement/src/v2-manifest-validation.ts:656-658`
  requires the evidence file to bind `baselineAdditions`, `baselineRemovals`,
  and `baselineRenames` as empty arrays. The staged delta holds 255 additions,
  15 removals, and 162 renames, so such evidence would state a falsehood.

Both rules belong to the deferred follow-up of Review B F2. Green did not
write a review record and did not change the schema.

The committed manifest stays valid. The gate is a write-path control. The
validator did not change. The check under policy v2 exits 0 with
`additions=0`, `removals=0`, and `renames=0`.

The gate refuses every later v2 reconcile write while the committed manifest
holds a non-empty delta and no review record. The follow-up must land before
that route can write again.

